ated with Yajurveda). The classification code list includes \"veda\" but not upaveda. It's not exactly a vedanga. I think it can be classified under \"veda\" broadly? But it's a specific text on warfare. Alternatively, it's sometimes considered part of kalpa? No. I'll use [\"veda\"] as a catch-all? But it's more properly an auxiliary science. The list has \"ayurveda\" separately, so maybe Dhanurveda should be something else? No code for Upaveda. I'll classify as \"veda\" since it's a secondary veda. Or maybe \"kalpa\"? Kalpa deals with rituals. Not exactly. I'll just use [\"veda\"].\n\n7. \"Dhanvantarinighaṇṭu\" – A medical lexicon by Dhanvantari. So it's a nighaṇṭu (lexicon) of medical terms. Classification: nighantu. Also could be ayurveda. So [\"nighantu\", \"ayurveda\"].\n\n8. \"Divyāvadāna\" – A Buddhist text, collection of legends. So classification: buddhist. It is a type of avadāna literature. So [\"buddhist\"].\n\n9. \"Drāhyāyaṇaśrautasūtra\" – A śrautasūtra belonging to the Sāma Veda. So classification: shrautasutra.\n\n10. \"Garbhopaniṣat\" – An Upanishad dealing with embryo. So upanishad.\n\n11. \"Garuḍapurāṇa\" – One of the 18 Mahāpurāṇas. So purana.\n\n12. \"Gautamadharmasūtra\" – A dharmasūtra by Gautama. So dharmasutra.\n\n13. \"Gaṇakārikā\" – A work on grammar or philosophy? Gaṇakārikā is a text of the Pāśupata school. It's a philosophical work. Could be darshana? Also related to tantra or agama? Pāśupata is a Śaiva sect. Classification: darshana (as a philosophical system), also maybe agama/tantra. I'll use [\"darshana\"].\n\n14. \"Gheraṇḍasaṃhitā\" – A classical text on hatha yoga. So yoga. Also samhita (but not in the Vedic sense). The code \"samhita\" is for Vedic samhitas, not yoga samhitas. So just [\"yoga\"].\n\n15. \"Gobhilagṛhyasūtra\" – A gṛhyasūtra belonging to the Sāma Veda. So grihyasutra.\n\n16. \"Gokarṇapurāṇasāraḥ\" – \"Essence of the Gokarṇa Purāṇa\". So likely a purana (or a summary of a purana). Classification: purana.\n\n17. \"Go