ly science. But traditionally, it's a separate branch. Looking at the classification codes: we have \"kavya\" (poetry), \"nataka\" (drama), etc. Not directly. I think it's best classified as \"sutra\" but not in list. Maybe we can use \"nibandha\"? That means treatise, digest. Nibandha is a later genre, but Kāmasūtra is a sūtra. Perhaps we can use \"smriti\"? Smriti includes texts like Manusmṛti. Kāmasūtra is not a Dharmaśāstra. I'll look: the list includes \"tantra\" for Tantric texts, \"agama\" for Āgamas. No. Could it be \"kavya\"? It is a scientific treatise, not poetry. So maybe there is no perfect code. Since the list is from given classification codes, we must pick from that. I think \"smriti\" might be a broad category for all smriti texts, including Dharma, Artha, Kāma, Moksha. But traditionally, Smriti refers to Dharmaśāstra. However, sometimes Arthaśāstra and Kāmaśāstra are included. I'll check: Arthaśāstra is often classified as smriti? No, it's a separate śāstra. In the list, we have \"dharmasutra\" for Dharma. There is no \"arthasutra\" or \"kamasutra\". So likely Kāmasūtra would be a sūtra text outside these classes. But we must use given codes. Perhaps we can use \"nibandha\"? But Kāmasūtra is not a nibandha. It is a mūla text. Maybe we can use \"shastra\" but that's not a code. There is \"rasashastra\", \"ayurveda\", but not. I think the closest is \"smriti\"? Actually, many libraries classify it under \"Smriti\" or \"Dharma\" because it deals with social conduct. I'll go with \"smriti\". Alternatively, we could use \"kavya\" if we consider it a poetic work, but it's not. Better to use \"smriti\". I'll also consider \"commentary\"? No. So classification: smriti. But wait, Kāmasūtra is a sūtra, so it might be a \"sutra\" genre, but not in list. Since we have \"dharmasutra\", \"grihyasutra\", \"shrautasutra\", but no \"kamasutra\" code. So I'll use \"smriti\" as a broader class. Or maybe \"nibandha\"? No. I'll use \"smriti\". \n\n   Translation: Russian: \"Камасутра\", English: \"Kāmasūtra\". Well known, so just transliteration with translation? The title means \"Aphorisms on Love/Desire\". Russian: \"Камасутра\" (already loanword), English: \"The Kāmasūtra\" or \"Aphorisms on Love\". I'll put \"Камасутра\" and \"Kāmasūtra\".\n\n4. id: \"9587ca04-39e0-4048-a73c-e3f41ec0b4af\", title: \"Kātyāyanasmṛti\"\n   This is a smṛti text by Kātyāyana. So classification: smriti. Also dharmasutra? Smritis are dharmaśāstra. So codes: smriti, dharmasutra (since it's a smriti in sūtra style? Actually Kātyāyanasmṛti is in verse, not sūtra. Dharmasutra is specifically sūtra texts. Kātyāyana wrote both Śrautasūtra and Smṛti. The Smṛti is in verse, so it's not a dharmasutra but a smriti. So classification: smriti. Might also be considered dharmashastra but we don't have that code, we have smriti and dharmasutra. Since it's not a sutra, I'll use smriti. \n   Translation: Russian: \"Катьяяна-смрити\", English: \"Kātyāyana Smṛti\" or \"The Smṛti of Kātyāyana\".\n\n5. id: \"97e1518a-b864-4ab3-8028-85c0b21b9ba2\", title: \"Kātyāyanaśrautasūtra\"\n   This is a Śrautasūtra by Kātyāyana. So classification: shrautasutra. Also kalpa? Śrautasūtra is part of Kalpa Vedāṅga. So codes: shrautasutra, kalpa, vedanga. \n   Translation: Russian: \"Шраутасутра Катьяяны\", English: \"Kātyāyana Śrautasūtra\".\n\n6. id: \"26579a09-37d7-43d7-9e8c-13a6391ea142\", title: \"Kāvyādarśa\"\n   This is a work on poetics by Daṇḍin. It's a mirror to poetry. Classification: kavya? Actually, it's a treatise on poetics, so it's an alaṃkāra śāstra. So it's a śāstra. In the list, we have \"kavya\" for poetry itself, but this is about poetics. Could be \"kavya\" as a genre? Kāvyādarśa is a textbook on kāvya. I think it's best classified as \"kavya\"? But that's a broad class. Actually, Daṇḍin's Kāvyādarśa is considered a foundational text on Sanskrit poetics. So it's a śāstra. There is no \"alamkara\" code. But we have \"kavya\" as a literary category. However, it's not a poem, it's a treatise. We could use \"commentary\"? No. Perhaps \"nibandha\"? That's a digest. But Kāvyādarśa is a systematic treatise. I'll classify as \"kavya\" because it deals with kāvya, and the code \"kavya\" might encompass works on poetics. Many catalogs put it under \"Poetry\" or \"Kāvya\". So I'll use \"kavya\". Maybe also \"shastra\" but not available. I'll use \"kavya\". \n   Translation: Russian: \"Кавьядарша\" (\"Зеркало поэзии\"), English: \"Kāvyādarśa\" (\"Mirror of Poetry\"). So Russian: \"Кавьядарша (Зеркало поэзии)\", but I'll just put the translation: \"Зеркало поэзии\" or \"Кавьядарша\". I'll provide both? The field is \"title_ru\", so I can write: \"Зеркало поэзии (Кавьядарша)\". But let's keep concise. I'll do: Russian: \"Кавьядарша\" is often left as is. But to translate: \"Зеркало поэзии\". I'll use \"Кавьядарша\" as it's a proper name, but instruction says translate. I'll put meaning. So Russian: \"Зеркало поэзии\", English: \"Mirror of Poetry\".\n\n7. id: \"55ef9d13-39c5-448a-8674-a30faf18e4e9\", title: \"Kāvyālaṃkāra\"\n   This is a work on poetics by Rudraṭa or someone? Actually, there are multiple Kāvyālaṃkāra works, e.g., by Bhāmaha. It's a treatise on poetic ornaments. So classification: kavya (as a poetic treatise). Same reasoning as above. Use \"kavya\".\n   Translation: Russian: \"Кавьяланкара\" or \"Поэтические украшения\", English: \"Kāvyālaṃkāra\" (\"Ornament of Poetry\" or \"Poetic Ornaments\"). So Russian: \"Поэтические украшения\", English: \"Ornament of Poetry\". But \"alaṃkāra\" means ornament. So I'll put: Russian: \"Кавьяланкара (Поэтические украшения)\", but simpler: \"Поэтические украшения\".\n\n8. id: \"62757dc1-5584-48aa-9b6a-0e1936b62abf\", title: \"Kāvyālaṃkāravṛtti\"\n   This is a commentary on Kāvyālaṃkāra. Vṛtti means commentary. So classification: commentary, vrtti (since it's a vṛtti specifically), and also kavya (since it's on poetics). Use codes: commentary, vrtti (we have \"vrtti\" as a code), and maybe \"kavya\". So: vrtti, commentary, kavya.\n   Translation: Russian: \"Комментарий к Кавьяланкаре\", English: \"A Commentary on Kāvyālaṃkāra\". Or more specifically: \"Kāvyālaṃkāravṛtti\" could be translated as \"The Vṛtti on the Ornament of Poetry\". So Russian: \"Вритти на Кавьяланкару\", English: \"The Vṛtti on Kāvyālaṃkāra\". I'll put: Russian: \"Вритти на «Кавьяланкару»\", English: \"The Vṛtti on the Kāvyālaṃkāra\".\n\n9. id: \"bf2d0ead-f478-4e8e-bd85-0345b2c1cdcf\", title: \"Kāśikāvṛtti\"\n   This is a famous commentary on Pāṇini's Aṣṭādhyāyī by Jayāditya and Vāmana. So it's a vyakarana commentary. Classification: vyakarana, commentary, vrtti (specific type). Use: vyakarana, commentary, vrtti.\n   Translation: Russian: \"Кашика-вритти\" (the name is often untranslated). \"Kāśikā\" refers to the city of Kashi (Varanasi). So it's \"The Vārāṇasī Commentary\". Russian: \"Варанаси-комментарий\" or \"Кашика-вритти\". I'll use: \"Кашика-вритти (Варанасийский комментарий)\". But to keep simple: Russian: \"Кашика-вритти\", English: \"Kāśikāvṛtti\" (The Vṛtti from Kāśī). Or translate: \"The Kāśī Commentary\".\n\n10. id: \"2e86bc38-311d-48b1-ba19-8b8fdc5cb64d\", title: \"Kāṭhakagṛhyasūtra\"\n    This is a Gṛhyasūtra belonging to the Kāṭhaka school of Yajurveda. Classification: grihyasutra, kalpa, vedanga.\n    Translation: Russian: \"Катхака-грихьясутра\", English: \"Kāṭhaka Gṛhyasūtra\" or \"The Gṛhyasūtra of the Kāṭhaka School\".\n\n11. id: \"15f195c9-c36f-485b-a94f-6c5abdf821a9\", title: \"Kāṭhakasaṃhitā\"\n    This is the Saṃhitā of the Kāṭhaka recension of the Yajurveda. Classification: samhita, veda.\n    Translation: Russian: \"Катхака-самхита\", English: \"Kāṭhaka Saṃhitā\" or \"The Saṃhitā of the Kāṭhaka School\".\n\n12. id: \"068e1a2f-ed1c-4887-9920-2b9ae6f4ddc1\", title: \"Kūrmapurāṇa\"\n    This is a Purāṇa. Classification: purana.\n    Translation: Russian: \"Курма-пурана\", English: \"The Kūrma Purāṇa\" or \"The Purāṇa of the Tortoise\".\n\n13. id: \"2518e1b1-90c1-4e2c-9a34-bbda8737554d\", title: \"Kṛṣiparāśara\"\n    This is a treatise on agriculture by Parāśara. \"Kṛṣi\" means agriculture. So it's a work on agriculture. Classification: maybe ayurveda? No, it's agriculture. Not in the list? We have ayurveda (medicine), but not vrikshayurveda or krishi. Could it be smriti? Sometimes agricultural texts are included in Smriti as part of dharma (varta). I'll classify as smriti? Or maybe as nibandha? It is a śāstra. Since there is no specific code, I'll use \"smriti\" as a broad class for traditional law and customs including livelihood. Alternatively, we could use \"nibandha\". But Parāśara is a smriti author, and Kṛṣiparāśara is a text on agriculture attributed to Parāśara. It might be considered a upaveda. But we don't have. I'll use \"smriti\". \n    Translation: Russian: \"Кришипарашара\" (\"Земледелие Парашары\"), English: \"Kṛṣiparāśara\" (\"Agriculture by Parāśara\").\n\n14. id: \"d4e7e422-9d38-41d4-abb0-92133469e08d\", title: \"Kṛṣṇāmṛtamahārṇava\"\n    This is a stotra work? Or a compendium on Krishna? \"Kṛṣṇāmṛta-mahā-arṇava\" means \"The Great Ocean of the Nectar of Krishna\". It is a devotional text. Could be a stotra collection. Classification: stotra? Possibly also kavya if it's poetry. But likely a bhakti text. We have \"stotra\" code, so I'll use stotra. Also maybe \"kavya\" if it's poetic. I'll use stotra and kavya.\n    Translation: Russian: \"Кришнамритамахарнава\" (\"Великий океан нектара Кришны\"), English: \"The Great Ocean of the Nectar of Krishna\".\n\n15. id: \"84ba5202-1901-4164-b2c2-9e2cf91bd384\", title: \"Lalitavistara\"\n    This is a Buddhist text belonging to the Mahāyāna sūtras. It is a biography of the Buddha. Classification: buddhist. Also could be considered a sūtra (buddhist sutra). So code: buddhist.\n    Translation: Russian: \"Лалитавистара\", English: \"Lalitavistara\" (The Detailed Account of the Play [of the Buddha]).\n\n16. id: \"45177a71-8bf7-4634-9fd6-d120f9bbd062\", title: \"Laṅkāvatārasūtra\"\n    A Buddhist Mahāyāna sūtra. Classification: buddhist.\n    Translation: Russian: \"Ланкаватара-сутра\", English: \"Laṅkāvatāra Sūtra\" (The Sūtra of the Descent into Laṅkā).\n\n17. id: \"b58e4246-b0d0-4cd2-aabd-3b9249f88ea6\", title: \"Liṅgapurāṇa\"\n    A Purāṇa devoted to the liṅga of Śiva. Classification: purana.\n    Translation: Russian: \"Линга-пурана\", English: \"The Liṅga Purāṇa\".\n\n18. id: \"149e9d0a-79f1-40ea-8121-84a76ec3b298\", title: \"Madanapālanighaṇṭu\"\n    This is a nighaṇṭu (lexicon) on medicinal plants and substances by Madanapāla. It is a work on Ayurveda. Classification: nighantu, ayurveda. Also kosha? Nighaṇṭu is a type of kośa, but we have separate \"nighantu\" code. Use: nighantu, ayurveda.\n    Translation: Russian: \"Маданапала-нигханту\", English: \"The Nighaṇṭu of Madanapāla\" or \"Madanapāla's Nighaṇṭu\".\n\n19. id: \"75194ad4-e70e-44a7-bbb3-8825aa93eb0e\", title: \"Mahābhārata\"\n    The great epic. Classification: itihasa (history), also mahakavya? It is considered both itihāsa and kāvya. So codes: itihasa, mahakavya (since it's a great epic poem). Actually, it is explicitly classified as itihāsa. And it's also a kāvya, some say it's a mahākāvya. So I'll use itihasa and mahakavya.\n    Translation: Russian: \"Махабхарата\", English: \"Mahābhārata\".\n\n20. id: \"1c8b63dd-8117-4cdd-80d5-8e512fadf8fb\", title: \"Mahācīnatantra\"\n    This is a Tantric text. \"Mahācīna\" means \"Great China\". So it's a text on Tantra, possibly related to the Vajrayana or a particular tradition. Classification: tantra.\n    Translation: Russian: \"Махачина-тантра\", English: \"The Mahācīna Tantra\" (The Tantra of the Great Use or The Chinese Tantra). Actually, \"Cīna\" can mean a kind of millet or something, but commonly it means China. So \"Great Chinese Tantra\" or \"Tantra of the Great Cina\". Russian: \"Махачина-тантра\".\n\n21. id: \"ef1e3c4d-6a96-462b-885a-92ed0d792219\", title: \"Maitrāyaṇīsaṃhitā\"\n    Saṃhitā of the Maitrāyaṇīya school of Yajurveda. Classification: samhita, veda.\n    Translation: Russian: \"Майтраяни-самхита\", English: \"Maitrāyaṇī Saṃhitā\".\n\n22. id: \"85575161-e515-4959-b66b-c43e3b03f608\", title: \"Manusmṛti\"\n    The famous law code. Classification: smriti, dharmasutra? Actually, it's in verse, so smriti. But sometimes dharmasutra is for sūtra texts. So I'll use smriti. Also could be dharmasutra? No, it's a smriti. Code: smriti.\n    Translation: Russian: \"Ману-смрити\" (or \"Законы Ману\"), English: \"The Laws of Manu\" or \"Manusmṛti\".\n\n23. id: \"4a9a7561-2650-43f6-b1d5-67e062f59e14\", title: \"Matsyapurāṇa\"\n    A Purāṇa. Classification: purana.\n    Translation: Russian: \"Матсья-пурана\", English: \"The Matsya Purāṇa\" (The Fish Purāṇa).\n\n24. id: \"c4986d9d-a912-4f05-82a5-43c580a16463\", title: \"Maṇimāhātmya\"\n    This is a text glorifying a particular jewel (maṇi) or perhaps a deity? \"Māhātmya\" means \"greatness, glorification\". It is a section of a Purāṇa or a separate text. Often māhātmyas are part of Purāṇas. Classification: purana? Or stotra? It is a eulogy. So classification: stotra, and maybe purana if it's from a Purāṇa. But as a standalone, it's a stotra type. I'll use stotra.\n    Translation: Russian: \"Манимахатмья\", English: \"The Glory of the Jewel\" or \"Maṇimāhātmya\".\n\n25. id: \"eb983954-07dd-4180-8e06-b8e0ec589233\", title: \"Meghadūta\"\n    This is a famous lyrical poem by Kālidāsa. It's a dūtakāvya (messenger poem). Classification: dutakavya, kavya.\n    Translation: Russian: \"Мегхадута\" (\"Облако-вестник\"), English: \"The Cloud Messenger\".\n\n26. id: \"f0e4b250-61f0-419f-9fbb-2cca76896e03\", title: \"Mugdhāvabodhinī\"\n    This is a commentary; \"mugdha\" means \"simple, charming\", \"avabodhinī\" means \"awakening, understanding\". Often this is a title of a commentary on a grammatical or literary work. For example, there is a Mugdhāvabodhinī on the Mugdhabodha grammar. But the title itself is a commentary. It might be a vyakarana commentary. Classification: commentary, possibly vyakarana. Since we don't know which text it comments on, but the name suggests a commentary. So use: commentary, vrtti? It's an avabodhinī, which is a type of explanation. Use commentary.\n    Translation: Russian: \"Мугдхавабодхини\", English: \"Mugdhāvabodhinī\" (The Enlightener of the Simple). Or \"Пробуждающая понимание у наивных\". I'll put: \"Мугдхавабодхини (Пояснение для несведущих)\".\n\n27. id: \"c3359d2a-a226-4bb9-840b-75f0864b37ca\", title: \"Mukundamālā\"\n    This is a stotra by Kulaśekhara Āḻvār, a devotional poem to Krishna (Mukunda). \"Mālā\" means garland. So a garland of hymns to Mukunda. Classification: stotra, kavya (since it's poetry).\n    Translation: Russian: \"Мукундамала\", English: \"The Garland [of Hymns] to Mukunda\".\n\n28. id: \"62f8e4b3-749e-42a7-977d-b630bfa0fa9e\", title: \"Muṇḍakopaniṣad\"\n    One of the principal Upaniṣads. Classification: upanishad.\n    Translation: Russian: \"Мундака-упанишада\", English: \"The Muṇḍaka Upaniṣad\".\n\n29. id: \"4507f65e-cb0c-4a72-9c9a-14131a474bb6\", title: \"Mānavagṛhyasūtra\"\n    Gṛhyasūtra of the Mānava school of the Black Yajurveda? Actually, Mānava means belonging to Manu? Wait, there is a Mānava Gṛhyasūtra belonging to the Maitrāyaṇīya school? Actually, Mānava is a branch of Yajurveda. So it's a Gṛhyasūtra. Classification: grihyasutra, kalpa, vedanga.\n    Translation: Russian: \"Манава-грихьясутра\", English: \"Mānava Gṛhyasūtra\".\n\n30. id: \"f6a1a326-1fce-4529-b38e-02f5f32abd9c\", title: \"Mānavaśrautasūtra\"\n    Śrautasūtra of the Mānava school. Classification: shrautasutra, kalpa, vedanga.\n    Translation: Russian: \"Манава-шраутасутра\", English: \"Mānava Śrautasūtra\".\n\n31. id: \"880c1e2a-3b33-48d6-80aa-a573c7223796\", title: \"Mātṛkābhedatantra\"\n    A Tantric text dealing with the distinctions of the mothers (Mātṛkās). Classification: tantra.\n    Translation: Russian: \"Матрикабхеда-тантра\", English: \"The Mātṛkābheda Tantra\" (The Tantra of the Differentiation of the Mothers).\n\n32. id: \"956a57da-0234-4818-9b82-4d6b8402cc5c\", title: \"Mīmāṃsāsūtrabhāṣya\"\n    This is the Bhāṣya on the Mīmāṃsā Sūtras by Śabara. Classification: mimamsa, bhashya, commentary.\n    Translation: Russian: \"Бхашья на «Миманса-сутры»\", English: \"The Mīmāṃsāsūtrabhāṣya\" (The Commentary on the Mīmāṃsā Sūtras). Or simply \"Mīmāṃsā Bhāṣya\".\n\n33. id: \"f9127683-2df7-4863-9641-74f5e01220f4\", title: \"Mūlamadhyamakārikāḥ\"\n    This is the fundamental text of Mādhyamaka Buddhism by Nāgārjuna. Classification: buddhist. It is a philosophical treatise. Also could be considered a śāstra. Since it's a Buddhist text, code: buddhist.\n    Translation: Russian: \"Муламадхьямака-карики\", English: \"Mūlamadhyamakakārikā\" (Fundamental Verses on the Middle Way).\n\n34. id: \"055f03a4-89f7-4883-926f-900a05816953\", title: \"Mṛgendratantra\"\n    A Tantric text. Classification: tantra.\n    Translation: Russian: \"Мригендра-тантра\", English: \"The Mṛgendra Tantra\" (The Tantra of the Lord of Animals, i.e., Śiva?).\n\n35. id: \"53358f7f-54e4-4dda-b163-3dfecc3b0159\", title: \"Mṛgendraṭīkā\"\n    A commentary on the Mṛgendra Tantra. So classification: commentary, tika, tantra.\n    Translation: Russian: \"Тика на «Мригендра-тантру»\", English: \"The Ṭīkā on the Mṛgendra Tantra\".\n\n36. id: \"ca1962e9-e232-4032-9536-fbfa8da27d33\", title: \"Narasiṃhapurāṇa\"\n    A Purāṇa dedicated to Narasiṃha (the man-lion avatar). Classification: purana.\n    Translation: Russian: \"Нарасимха-пурана\", English: \"The Narasiṃha Purāṇa\".\n\n37. id: \"70c036a4-fa4e-469e-99d6-e4a5607b5b2f\", title: \"Narmamālā\"\n    \"Narma\" means \"sport, jest\", \"mālā\" garland. This could be a collection of humorous verses or a light-hearted poem. Classification: kavya (poetry), maybe shataka? Not exactly. I'll classify as kavya.\n    Translation: Russian: \"Нармамала\" (\"Гирлянда шуток\"), English: \"The Garland of Jests\" or \"The Chain of Humor\".\n\n38. id: \"68c42dc2-c1cc-43f0-821f-3e4ba9f86d2d\", title: \"Nibandhasaṃgraha\"\n    This means \"collection of nibandhas\" (digests or treatises). So it is a compilation of law digests or religious digests. Classification: nibandha, smriti? Since nibandhas often deal with dharma. So use nibandha, smriti.\n    Translation: Russian: \"Нибандха-санграха\" (\"Собрание рассуждений/трактатов\"), English: \"A Collection of Digests\" or \"Nibandhasaṃgraha\".\n\n39. id: \"2d389b1e-3766-49da-8558-4d566bd52fce\", title: \"Nighaṇṭuśeṣa\"\n    This is a supplement to the Nighaṇṭu (the Vedic lexicon by Yāska). So it's a nighantu, nirukta? Actually, it's part of the Nirukta tradition. Classification: nighantu, nirukta, vedanga (since Nirukta is a Vedāṅga).\n    Translation: Russian: \"Нигханту-шеша\" (\"Дополнение к Нигханту\"), English: \"The Supplemen t to the Nighaṇṭu\" or \"Nighaṇṭuśeṣa\".\n\n40. id: \"684374d4-f315-4fff-9211-c14e847d6c66\", title: \"Nirukta\"\n    Yāska's Nirukta, a commentary on the Nighaṇṭu and a treatise on etymology. Classification: nirukta, vedanga.\n    Translation: Russian: \"Нирукта\", English: \"Nirukta\".\n\n41. id: \"11ff1727-d8f4-47c6-b56c-d5146ccb38f7\", title: \"Nyāyabhāṣya\"\n    This is the Bhāṣya on the Nyāyasūtra by Vātsyāyana. Classification: nyaya, bhashya, commentary.\n    Translation: Russian: \"Ньяя-бхашья\", English: \"The Nyāyabhāṣya\" (The Commentary on the Nyāya Sūtras).\n\n42. id: \"002715f6-f675-4ec1-9a59-6966ebbaedbc\", title: \"Nyāyabindu\"\n    A Buddhist logical treatise by Dharmakīrti. Classification: buddhist, and it's a nyaya (logic) text. But since it's Buddhist logic, use buddhist, nyaya? We have both codes. So use: buddhist, nyaya.\n    Translation: Russian: \"Ньяя-бинду\" (\"Капля логики\"), English: \"The Drop of Logic\" or \"Nyāyabindu\".\n\n43. id: \"f1b4f911-7f76-41ae-abc4-8714785d8b71\", title: \"Nyāyasūtra\"\n    The foundational text of the Nyāya school by Gautama. Classification: nyaya, darshana (since it's a philosophical system). Use: nyaya.\n    Translation: Russian: \"Ньяя-сутры\", English: \"The Nyāya Sūtras\".\n\n44. id: \"14c70603-d15f-475f-86cc-79f37dee0b2b\", title: \"Nādabindūpaniṣat\"\n    A minor Upaniṣad, a Yoga Upaniṣad. Classification: upanishad, yoga (since it deals with nāda and bindu). Use: upanishad, yoga.\n    Translation: Russian: \"Нада-бинду-упанишада\", English: \"The Nādabindu Upaniṣad\".\n\n45. id: \"bac18679-91c8-4471-8aff-a04ba3732794\", title: \"Nāradasmṛti\"\n    A smṛti text by Nārada. Classification: smriti.\n    Translation: Russian: \"Нарада-смрити\", English: \"The Nārada Smṛti\".\n\n46. id: \"3143f36d-e1fb-447e-98c4-d14caf0920a2\", title: \"Nāḍīparīkṣā\"\n    This is a text on pulse examination, an Ayurvedic diagnostic method. Classification: ayurveda.\n    Translation: Russian: \"Нади-парикша\" (\"Исследование пульса\"), English: \"Examination of the Pulse\" or \"Nāḍīparīkṣā\".\n\n47. id: \"7910df8f-5c4a-4f33-ad07-4e2a86c2590d\", title: \"Nāṭyaśāstra\"\n    The foundational text on drama and performing arts by Bharata. Classification: nataka? Actually, it's a śāstra on nāṭya. We have \"nataka\" code for drama, but Nāṭyaśāstra is a treatise on dramaturgy. It can be classified under nataka or maybe kavya (since it's about poetry and drama). I'll use nataka, and also it's a śāstra. But we don't have a \"shastra\" code, but we can use \"nataka\" to indicate it's about drama. Some might classify as \"kavya\" but it's theoretical. I'll use \"nataka\".\n    Translation: Russian: \"Натьяшастра\", English: \"The Nāṭyaśāstra\" (The Treatise on Drama).\n\n48. id: \"1e19c8f7-da54-42db-90e6-3389f4ee8c4f\", title: \"Nāṭyaśāstravivṛti\"\n    A commentary on the Nāṭyaśāstra. Classification: commentary, vivriti (since it's a vivṛti), nataka (subject). So: commentary, vivriti, nataka.\n    Translation: Russian: \"Комментарий на «Натьяшастру»\", English: \"The Vivṛti on the Nāṭyaśāstra\" or \"Nāṭyaśāstravivṛti\".\n\n49. id: \"a777574c-e81b-4be9-9a61-901cfa010578\", title: \"Padārthacandrikā\"\n    This is a commentary. \"Padārtha\" means \"category, meaning of a word\", \"candrikā\" means \"moonlight\" (i.e., an illuminating commentary). It is often a title of a commentary on a grammatical or philosophical work. For example, there is a Padārthacandrikā on the Vākyapadīya or on a kośa. It could be a vyakarana or darshana commentary. Without more context, it's a commentary. Classification: commentary. Possibly vyakarana or nyaya? I'll use commentary.\n    Translation: Russian: \"Падартха-чандрика\" (\"Лунный свет категорий\"), English: \"The Moonlight on the Categories\" or \"Padārthacandrikā\".\n\n50. id: \"58011754-2306-4b2a-baec-fcdec1a845be\", title: \"Paramānandīyanāmamālā\"\n    This is a dictionary of synonyms or a thesaurus by Paramānanda. It's a kośa. \"Nāmamālā\" means \"garland of names\". So classification: kosha, nighantu? It's a type of nighaṇṭu. Use: kosha, nighantu.\n    Translation: Russian: \"Параманандия-намамала\", English: \"The Garland of Names by Paramānanda\" or \"Paramānandīyanāmamālā\".\n\nNow, I'll compile the JSON. Ensure all ids match and classification codes are arrays. Use the exact codes from the list.\n\nFor each, I'll output like:\n\n{\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"2c5a7983-2e2d-4dc3-8716-a0c75d641d22\",\n      \"title_sa_iast\": \"Kādambarīsvīkaraṇasūtramañjarī\",\n      \"title_ru\": \"Сутра-манджари о грамматическом использовании Кадамбари\",\n      \"title_en\": \"The Sutra Garland on the Grammatical Appropriation of Kādambarī\",\n      \"classification_codes\": [\"vyakarana\", \"commentary\"]\n    },\n    ... etc.\n  ]\n}\n\nI'll try to keep translations concise but meaningful. For well-known titles, I might use the standard English title.\n\nLet's produce final JSON.",
        "reasoning_details": [
          {
            "type": "reasoning.text",
            "text": "We are asked to process a list of Sanskrit works. For each, we need to provide: translation into Russian and English, and classification codes from the given list. We need to output JSON exactly as specified. Let's go one by one.\n\nWe'll create an array of results. For each work, we'll determine the appropriate classification codes.\n\nRemember: The JSON structure is:\n{\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"uuid_string\",\n      \"title_sa_iast\": \"original_title\",\n      \"title_ru\": \"translation_in_russian\",\n      \"title_en\": \"translation_in_english\",\n      \"classification_codes\": [\"code1\", \"code2\"]\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\nLet's process each work:\n\n1. id: \"2c5a7983-2e2d-4dc3-8716-a0c75d641d22\", title: \"Kādambarīsvīkaraṇasūtramañjarī\"\n   Meaning: This is a commentary on the Kādambarī (a prose romance). Svīkaraṇa means \"accepting\" or \"appropriation\", sūtramañjarī means \"collection of aphorisms\". So it's a commentary work. Might be a grammatical or literary commentary? Actually, Kādambarī is a kathā (story) by Bāṇabhaṭṭa. So this is likely a commentary on that work. Classification: commentary? Possibly tika or bhashya. It might be a vyakarana work? But title suggests it's a commentary on Kādambarī. I'll classify as commentary (using code \"commentary\") and maybe \"tika\" or \"bhashya\"? Since it's a mañjarī (blossom/collection) of sūtras about svīkaraṇa (appropriation) of Kādambarī, it might be a grammatical work on the language of Kādambarī? But Kādambarīsvīkaraṇa is a grammatical work by Bhānujī Dīkṣita? Let's think: I recall a work \"Kādambarīsvīkaraṇasūtramañjarī\" is a commentary on the \"Kādambarīsvīkaraṇa\" which is a grammatical treatise. Actually, Svīkaraṇa means \"taking possession\", and it's a grammatical term? Alternatively, \"Kādambarīsvīkaraṇa\" is a work that extracts grammatical rules from Kādambarī. And the Sūtramañjarī is a commentary on that. So it likely belongs to Vyākaraṇa (grammar). So classification: vyakarana, commentary, maybe tika. We'll use vyakarana and commentary.\n\n   Translation: \n   Russian: \"Кадамбарисвикаранасутраманджари\" (a commentary on grammatical sūtras from Kādambarī) — maybe translate as \"Собрание сутр о присвоении Кадамбари\" or something. Better: \"Кадамбарисвикарана-сутра-манджари\" (the title is often left transliterated). But we need translation. \"Kādambarīsvīkaraṇa\" means \"appropriation of Kādambarī\" (grammatical rules extracted from Kādambarī). \"Sūtramañjarī\" means \"cluster of sūtras\". So: Russian: \"Собрание сутр о грамматическом использовании [языка] «Кадамбари»\" or simpler: \"Маджари сутр о присвоении Кадамбари\". I'll try: \"Кадамбарисвикаранасутраманджари\" and in English: \"A Cluster of Sūtras on the Grammatical Appropriation of the Kādambarī\". But we need accurate translation. Let's see: Kādambarī is the title, svīkaraṇa is \"taking for oneself, appropriation\", sūtra-mañjarī \"collection of aphorisms\". So English: \"The Cluster of Aphorisms on the Appropriation of Kādambarī\". But it's a commentary. I'll put: Russian: \"Кадамбари-свикарана-сутра-манджари\" (maybe just transliteration is fine as it's a title). But instructions say: \"Translate the title into Russian and English\". So we should translate meaning. I'll do: Russian: \"Кадамбарисвикаранасутраманджари\" and explain in parentheses? But output should be plain text. I'll provide: Russian: \"Сутра-манджари о Кадамбарисвикаране\" or something. Better to keep standard transliteration? The instruction says \"translate\", so we give a translation, not just transliteration. But many Sanskrit titles are proper names and often left untranslated. However, we should attempt a meaningful translation. I'll try: English: \"The Garland of Aphorisms on the Grammatical Employment of the Kādambarī\". Russian: \"Гирлянда сутр о грамматическом использовании Кадамбари\". But \"mañjarī\" is often translated as \"cluster\" or \"garland\". I'll go with \"garland\" as it's poetic. But be consistent. I'll do: \"Kādambarīsvīkaraṇasūtramañjarī\" -> English: \"The Sutra Garland on the Grammatical Appropriation of the Kadambari\", Russian: \"Сутра-манджари о грамматическом присвоении Кадамбари\". Actually, \"svīkaraṇa\" in grammar means \"taking a word as one's own\", i.e., using it. So it's about extracting grammatical rules from Kadambari. I'll refine.\n\n   Classification: vyakarana and commentary (since it's a commentary on a vyakarana work). Possibly \"tika\" or \"bhashya\"? It's a mañjarī, which is a type of commentary. Use \"vyakarana\", \"commentary\". I'll also add \"tika\" as it's a subcommentary maybe.\n\n2. id: \"c3da8b12-6b23-45a7-8972-f45e4c23b0dd\", title: \"Kālikāpurāṇa\"\n   This is a Purāṇa. So classification: purana.\n   Translation: Russian: \"Калика-пурана\", English: \"The Kālikā Purāṇa\". Actually, it's a specific Purana dedicated to goddess Kālikā. So translate accordingly: Russian: \"Калика-пурана\" (or \"Пурана Калики\"), English: \"The Kālikā Purāṇa\" or \"The Purāṇa of Kālikā\".\n\n3. id: \"566a20e1-de08-4dea-8e05-068d681cf8f7\", title: \"Kāmasūtra\"\n   This is the famous treatise on love and sexuality. Classification: kavya? Actually, it's a śāstra. It's a smriti? No, it's a treatise on kāma (desire) by Vātsyāyana. It's considered a Kāmaśāstra, which is a genre within Dharma or Artha? Generally, it's classified under \"Kāmaśāstra\". In our list, we have categories like smriti? Smriti includes Dharmaśāstra, but Kāmasūtra is not Smriti strictly. We don't have a specific \"kama\" code. It might fall under \"shastra\" but not listed. Possibly \"nibandha\"? Not really. It can be considered a śāstra, and somewhere between smriti and kavya? Actually, Kāmasūtra is a sūtra text, so it's a sūtra work. In the given list, the closest might be \"tantra\"? No. Perhaps \"ayurveda\"? No. Wait, list includes: smriti (Dharmaśāstra), but Kāmaśāstra is not Smriti. However, some consider it part of Smriti because it's a worldly science. But traditionally, it's a separate branch. Looking at the classification codes: we have \"kavya\" (poetry), \"nataka\" (drama), etc. Not directly. I think it's best classified as \"sutra\" but not in list. Maybe we can use \"nibandha\"? That means treatise, digest. Nibandha is a later genre, but Kāmasūtra is a sūtra. Perhaps we can use \"smriti\"? Smriti includes texts like Manusmṛti. Kāmasūtra is not a Dharmaśāstra. I'll look: the list includes \"tantra\" for Tantric texts, \"agama\" for Āgamas. No. Could it be \"kavya\"? It is a scientific treatise, not poetry. So maybe there is no perfect code. Since the list is from given classification codes, we must pick from that. I think \"smriti\" might be a broad category for all smriti texts, including Dharma, Artha, Kāma, Moksha. But traditionally, Smriti refers to Dharmaśāstra. However, sometimes Arthaśāstra and Kāmaśāstra are included. I'll check: Arthaśāstra is often classified as smriti? No, it's a separate śāstra. In the list, we have \"dharmasutra\" for Dharma. There is no \"arthasutra\" or \"kamasutra\". So likely Kāmasūtra would be a sūtra text outside these classes. But we must use given codes. Perhaps we can use \"nibandha\"? But Kāmasūtra is not a nibandha. It is a mūla text. Maybe we can use \"shastra\" but that's not a code. There is \"rasashastra\", \"ayurveda\", but not. I think the closest is \"smriti\"? Actually, many libraries classify it under \"Smriti\" or \"Dharma\" because it deals with social conduct. I'll go with \"smriti\". Alternatively, we could use \"kavya\" if we consider it a poetic work, but it's not. Better to use \"smriti\". I'll also consider \"commentary\"? No. So classification: smriti. But wait, Kāmasūtra is a sūtra, so it might be a \"sutra\" genre, but not in list. Since we have \"dharmasutra\", \"grihyasutra\", \"shrautasutra\", but no \"kamasutra\" code. So I'll use \"smriti\" as a broader class. Or maybe \"nibandha\"? No. I'll use \"smriti\". \n\n   Translation: Russian: \"Камасутра\", English: \"Kāmasūtra\". Well known, so just transliteration with translation? The title means \"Aphorisms on Love/Desire\". Russian: \"Камасутра\" (already loanword), English: \"The Kāmasūtra\" or \"Aphorisms on Love\". I'll put \"Камасутра\" and \"Kāmasūtra\".\n\n4. id: \"9587ca04-39e0-4048-a73c-e3f41ec0b4af\", title: \"Kātyāyanasmṛti\"\n   This is a smṛti text by Kātyāyana. So classification: smriti. Also dharmasutra? Smritis are dharmaśāstra. So codes: smriti, dharmasutra (since it's a smriti in sūtra style? Actually Kātyāyanasmṛti is in verse, not sūtra. Dharmasutra is specifically sūtra texts. Kātyāyana wrote both Śrautasūtra and Smṛti. The Smṛti is in verse, so it's not a dharmasutra but a smriti. So classification: smriti. Might also be considered dharmashastra but we don't have that code, we have smriti and dharmasutra. Since it's not a sutra, I'll use smriti. \n   Translation: Russian: \"Катьяяна-смрити\", English: \"Kātyāyana Smṛti\" or \"The Smṛti of Kātyāyana\".\n\n5. id: \"97e1518a-b864-4ab3-8028-85c0b21b9ba2\", title: \"Kātyāyanaśrautasūtra\"\n   This is a Śrautasūtra by Kātyāyana. So classification: shrautasutra. Also kalpa? Śrautasūtra is part of Kalpa Vedāṅga. So codes: shrautasutra, kalpa, vedanga. \n   Translation: Russian: \"Шраутасутра Катьяяны\", English: \"Kātyāyana Śrautasūtra\".\n\n6. id: \"26579a09-37d7-43d7-9e8c-13a6391ea142\", title: \"Kāvyādarśa\"\n   This is a work on poetics by Daṇḍin. It's a mirror to poetry. Classification: kavya? Actually, it's a treatise on poetics, so it's an alaṃkāra śāstra. So it's a śāstra. In the list, we have \"kavya\" for poetry itself, but this is about poetics. Could be \"kavya\" as a genre? Kāvyādarśa is a textbook on kāvya. I think it's best classified as \"kavya\"? But that's a broad class. Actually, Daṇḍin's Kāvyādarśa is considered a foundational text on Sanskrit poetics. So it's a śāstra. There is no \"alamkara\" code. But we have \"kavya\" as a literary category. However, it's not a poem, it's a treatise. We could use \"commentary\"? No. Perhaps \"nibandha\"? That's a digest. But Kāvyādarśa is a systematic treatise. I'll classify as \"kavya\" because it deals with kāvya, and the code \"kavya\" might encompass works on poetics. Many catalogs put it under \"Poetry\" or \"Kāvya\". So I'll use \"kavya\". Maybe also \"shastra\" but not available. I'll use \"kavya\". \n   Translation: Russian: \"Кавьядарша\" (\"Зеркало поэзии\"), English: \"Kāvyādarśa\" (\"Mirror of Poetry\"). So Russian: \"Кавьядарша (Зеркало поэзии)\", but I'll just put the translation: \"Зеркало поэзии\" or \"Кавьядарша\". I'll provide both? The field is \"title_ru\", so I can write: \"Зеркало поэзии (Кавьядарша)\". But let's keep concise. I'll do: Russian: \"Кавьядарша\" is often left as is. But to translate: \"Зеркало поэзии\". I'll use \"Кавьядарша\" as it's a proper name, but instruction says translate. I'll put meaning. So Russian: \"Зеркало поэзии\", English: \"Mirror of Poetry\".\n\n7. id: \"55ef9d13-39c5-448a-8674-a30faf18e4e9\", title: \"Kāvyālaṃkāra\"\n   This is a work on poetics by Rudraṭa or someone? Actually, there are multiple Kāvyālaṃkāra works, e.g., by Bhāmaha. It's a treatise on poetic ornaments. So classification: kavya (as a poetic treatise). Same reasoning as above. Use \"kavya\".\n   Translation: Russian: \"Кавьяланкара\" or \"Поэтические украшения\", English: \"Kāvyālaṃkāra\" (\"Ornament of Poetry\" or \"Poetic Ornaments\"). So Russian: \"Поэтические украшения\", English: \"Ornament of Poetry\". But \"alaṃkāra\" means ornament. So I'll put: Russian: \"Кавьяланкара (Поэтические украшения)\", but simpler: \"Поэтические украшения\".\n\n8. id: \"62757dc1-5584-48aa-9b6a-0e1936b62abf\", title: \"Kāvyālaṃkāravṛtti\"\n   This is a commentary on Kāvyālaṃkāra. Vṛtti means commentary. So classification: commentary, vrtti (since it's a vṛtti specifically), and also kavya (since it's on poetics). Use codes: commentary, vrtti (we have \"vrtti\" as a code), and maybe \"kavya\". So: vrtti, commentary, kavya.\n   Translation: Russian: \"Комментарий к Кавьяланкаре\", English: \"A Commentary on Kāvyālaṃkāra\". Or more specifically: \"Kāvyālaṃkāravṛtti\" could be translated as \"The Vṛtti on the Ornament of Poetry\". So Russian: \"Вритти на Кавьяланкару\", English: \"The Vṛtti on Kāvyālaṃkāra\". I'll put: Russian: \"Вритти на «Кавьяланкару»\", English: \"The Vṛtti on the Kāvyālaṃkāra\".\n\n9. id: \"bf2d0ead-f478-4e8e-bd85-0345b2c1cdcf\", title: \"Kāśikāvṛtti\"\n   This is a famous commentary on Pāṇini's Aṣṭādhyāyī by Jayāditya and Vāmana. So it's a vyakarana commentary. Classification: vyakarana, commentary, vrtti (specific type). Use: vyakarana, commentary, vrtti.\n   Translation: Russian: \"Кашика-вритти\" (the name is often untranslated). \"Kāśikā\" refers to the city of Kashi (Varanasi). So it's \"The Vārāṇasī Commentary\". Russian: \"Варанаси-комментарий\" or \"Кашика-вритти\". I'll use: \"Кашика-вритти (Варанасийский комментарий)\". But to keep simple: Russian: \"Кашика-вритти\", English: \"Kāśikāvṛtti\" (The Vṛtti from Kāśī). Or translate: \"The Kāśī Commentary\".\n\n10. id: \"2e86bc38-311d-48b1-ba19-8b8fdc5cb64d\", title: \"Kāṭhakagṛhyasūtra\"\n    This is a Gṛhyasūtra belonging to the Kāṭhaka school of Yajurveda. Classification: grihyasutra, kalpa, vedanga.\n    Translation: Russian: \"Катхака-грихьясутра\", English: \"Kāṭhaka Gṛhyasūtra\" or \"The Gṛhyasūtra of the Kāṭhaka School\".\n\n11. id: \"15f195c9-c36f-485b-a94f-6c5abdf821a9\", title: \"Kāṭhakasaṃhitā\"\n    This is the Saṃhitā of the Kāṭhaka recension of the Yajurveda. Classification: samhita, veda.\n    Translation: Russian: \"Катхака-самхита\", English: \"Kāṭhaka Saṃhitā\" or \"The Saṃhitā of the Kāṭhaka School\".\n\n12. id: \"068e1a2f-ed1c-4887-9920-2b9ae6f4ddc1\", title: \"Kūrmapurāṇa\"\n    This is a Purāṇa. Classification: purana.\n    Translation: Russian: \"Курма-пурана\", English: \"The Kūrma Purāṇa\" or \"The Purāṇa of the Tortoise\".\n\n13. id: \"2518e1b1-90c1-4e2c-9a34-bbda8737554d\", title: \"Kṛṣiparāśara\"\n    This is a treatise on agriculture by Parāśara. \"Kṛṣi\" means agriculture. So it's a work on agriculture. Classification: maybe ayurveda? No, it's agriculture. Not in the list? We have ayurveda (medicine), but not vrikshayurveda or krishi. Could it be smriti? Sometimes agricultural texts are included in Smriti as part of dharma (varta). I'll classify as smriti? Or maybe as nibandha? It is a śāstra. Since there is no specific code, I'll use \"smriti\" as a broad class for traditional law and customs including livelihood. Alternatively, we could use \"nibandha\". But Parāśara is a smriti author, and Kṛṣiparāśara is a text on agriculture attributed to Parāśara. It might be considered a upaveda. But we don't have. I'll use \"smriti\". \n    Translation: Russian: \"Кришипарашара\" (\"Земледелие Парашары\"), English: \"Kṛṣiparāśara\" (\"Agriculture by Parāśara\").\n\n14. id: \"d4e7e422-9d38-41d4-abb0-92133469e08d\", title: \"Kṛṣṇāmṛtamahārṇava\"\n    This is a stotra work? Or a compendium on Krishna? \"Kṛṣṇāmṛta-mahā-arṇava\" means \"The Great Ocean of the Nectar of Krishna\". It is a devotional text. Could be a stotra collection. Classification: stotra? Possibly also kavya if it's poetry. But likely a bhakti text. We have \"stotra\" code, so I'll use stotra. Also maybe \"kavya\" if it's poetic. I'll use stotra and kavya.\n    Translation: Russian: \"Кришнамритамахарнава\" (\"Великий океан нектара Кришны\"), English: \"The Great Ocean of the Nectar of Krishna\".\n\n15. id: \"84ba5202-1901-4164-b2c2-9e2cf91bd384\", title: \"Lalitavistara\"\n    This is a Buddhist text belonging to the Mahāyāna sūtras. It is a biography of the Buddha. Classification: buddhist. Also could be considered a sūtra (buddhist sutra). So code: buddhist.\n    Translation: Russian: \"Лалитавистара\", English: \"Lalitavistara\" (The Detailed Account of the Play [of the Buddha]).\n\n16. id: \"45177a71-8bf7-4634-9fd6-d120f9bbd062\", title: \"Laṅkāvatārasūtra\"\n    A Buddhist Mahāyāna sūtra. Classification: buddhist.\n    Translation: Russian: \"Ланкаватара-сутра\", English: \"Laṅkāvatāra Sūtra\" (The Sūtra of the Descent into Laṅkā).\n\n17. id: \"b58e4246-b0d0-4cd2-aabd-3b9249f88ea6\", title: \"Liṅgapurāṇa\"\n    A Purāṇa devoted to the liṅga of Śiva. Classification: purana.\n    Translation: Russian: \"Линга-пурана\", English: \"The Liṅga Purāṇa\".\n\n18. id: \"149e9d0a-79f1-40ea-8121-84a76ec3b298\", title: \"Madanapālanighaṇṭu\"\n    This is a nighaṇṭu (lexicon) on medicinal plants and substances by Madanapāla. It is a work on Ayurveda. Classification: nighantu, ayurveda. Also kosha? Nighaṇṭu is a type of kośa, but we have separate \"nighantu\" code. Use: nighantu, ayurveda.\n    Translation: Russian: \"Маданапала-нигханту\", English: \"The Nighaṇṭu of Madanapāla\" or \"Madanapāla's Nighaṇṭu\".\n\n19. id: \"75194ad4-e70e-44a7-bbb3-8825aa93eb0e\", title: \"Mahābhārata\"\n    The great epic. Classification: itihasa (history), also mahakavya? It is considered both itihāsa and kāvya. So codes: itihasa, mahakavya (since it's a great epic poem). Actually, it is explicitly classified as itihāsa. And it's also a kāvya, some say it's a mahākāvya. So I'll use itihasa and mahakavya.\n    Translation: Russian: \"Махабхарата\", English: \"Mahābhārata\".\n\n20. id: \"1c8b63dd-8117-4cdd-80d5-8e512fadf8fb\", title: \"Mahācīnatantra\"\n    This is a Tantric text. \"Mahācīna\" means \"Great China\". So it's a text on Tantra, possibly related to the Vajrayana or a particular tradition. Classification: tantra.\n    Translation: Russian: \"Махачина-тантра\", English: \"The Mahācīna Tantra\" (The Tantra of the Great Use or The Chinese Tantra). Actually, \"Cīna\" can mean a kind of millet or something, but commonly it means China. So \"Great Chinese Tantra\" or \"Tantra of the Great Cina\". Russian: \"Махачина-тантра\".\n\n21. id: \"ef1e3c4d-6a96-462b-885a-92ed0d792219\", title: \"Maitrāyaṇīsaṃhitā\"\n    Saṃhitā of the Maitrāyaṇīya school of Yajurveda. Classification: samhita, veda.\n    Translation: Russian: \"Майтраяни-самхита\", English: \"Maitrāyaṇī Saṃhitā\".\n\n22. id: \"85575161-e515-4959-b66b-c43e3b03f608\", title: \"Manusmṛti\"\n    The famous law code. Classification: smriti, dharmasutra? Actually, it's in verse, so smriti. But sometimes dharmasutra is for sūtra texts. So I'll use smriti. Also could be dharmasutra? No, it's a smriti. Code: smriti.\n    Translation: Russian: \"Ману-смрити\" (or \"Законы Ману\"), English: \"The Laws of Manu\" or \"Manusmṛti\".\n\n23. id: \"4a9a7561-2650-43f6-b1d5-67e062f59e14\", title: \"Matsyapurāṇa\"\n    A Purāṇa. Classification: purana.\n    Translation: Russian: \"Матсья-пурана\", English: \"The Matsya Purāṇa\" (The Fish Purāṇa).\n\n24. id: \"c4986d9d-a912-4f05-82a5-43c580a16463\", title: \"Maṇimāhātmya\"\n    This is a text glorifying a particular jewel (maṇi) or perhaps a deity? \"Māhātmya\" means \"greatness, glorification\". It is a section of a Purāṇa or a separate text. Often māhātmyas are part of Purāṇas. Classification: purana? Or stotra? It is a eulogy. So classification: stotra, and maybe purana if it's from a Purāṇa. But as a standalone, it's a stotra type. I'll use stotra.\n    Translation: Russian: \"Манимахатмья\", English: \"The Glory of the Jewel\" or \"Maṇimāhātmya\".\n\n25. id: \"eb983954-07dd-4180-8e06-b8e0ec589233\", title: \"Meghadūta\"\n    This is a famous lyrical poem by Kālidāsa. It's a dūtakāvya (messenger poem). Classification: dutakavya, kavya.\n    Translation: Russian: \"Мегхадута\" (\"Облако-вестник\"), English: \"The Cloud Messenger\".\n\n26. id: \"f0e4b250-61f0-419f-9fbb-2cca76896e03\", title: \"Mugdhāvabodhinī\"\n    This is a commentary; \"mugdha\" means \"simple, charming\", \"avabodhinī\" means \"awakening, understanding\". Often this is a title of a commentary on a grammatical or literary work. For example, there is a Mugdhāvabodhinī on the Mugdhabodha grammar. But the title itself is a commentary. It might be a vyakarana commentary. Classification: commentary, possibly vyakarana. Since we don't know which text it comments on, but the name suggests a commentary. So use: commentary, vrtti? It's an avabodhinī, which is a type of explanation. Use commentary.\n    Translation: Russian: \"Мугдхавабодхини\", English: \"Mugdhāvabodhinī\" (The Enlightener of the Simple). Or \"Пробуждающая понимание у наивных\". I'll put: \"Мугдхавабодхини (Пояснение для несведущих)\".\n\n27. id: \"c3359d2a-a226-4bb9-840b-75f0864b37ca\", title: \"Mukundamālā\"\n    This is a stotra by Kulaśekhara Āḻvār, a devotional poem to Krishna (Mukunda). \"Mālā\" means garland. So a garland of hymns to Mukunda. Classification: stotra, kavya (since it's poetry).\n    Translation: Russian: \"Мукундамала\", English: \"The Garland [of Hymns] to Mukunda\".\n\n28. id: \"62f8e4b3-749e-42a7-977d-b630bfa0fa9e\", title: \"Muṇḍakopaniṣad\"\n    One of the principal Upaniṣads. Classification: upanishad.\n    Translation: Russian: \"Мундака-упанишада\", English: \"The Muṇḍaka Upaniṣad\".\n\n29. id: \"4507f65e-cb0c-4a72-9c9a-14131a474bb6\", title: \"Mānavagṛhyasūtra\"\n    Gṛhyasūtra of the Mānava school of the Black Yajurveda? Actually, Mānava means belonging to Manu? Wait, there is a Mānava Gṛhyasūtra belonging to the Maitrāyaṇīya school? Actually, Mānava is a branch of Yajurveda. So it's a Gṛhyasūtra. Classification: grihyasutra, kalpa, vedanga.\n    Translation: Russian: \"Манава-грихьясутра\", English: \"Mānava Gṛhyasūtra\".\n\n30. id: \"f6a1a326-1fce-4529-b38e-02f5f32abd9c\", title: \"Mānavaśrautasūtra\"\n    Śrautasūtra of the Mānava school. Classification: shrautasutra, kalpa, vedanga.\n    Translation: Russian: \"Манава-шраутасутра\", English: \"Mānava Śrautasūtra\".\n\n31. id: \"880c1e2a-3b33-48d6-80aa-a573c7223796\", title: \"Mātṛkābhedatantra\"\n    A Tantric text dealing with the distinctions of the mothers (Mātṛkās). Classification: tantra.\n    Translation: Russian: \"Матрикабхеда-тантра\", English: \"The Mātṛkābheda Tantra\" (The Tantra of the Differentiation of the Mothers).\n\n32. id: \"956a57da-0234-4818-9b82-4d6b8402cc5c\", title: \"Mīmāṃsāsūtrabhāṣya\"\n    This is the Bhāṣya on the Mīmāṃsā Sūtras by Śabara. Classification: mimamsa, bhashya, commentary.\n    Translation: Russian: \"Бхашья на «Миманса-сутры»\", English: \"The Mīmāṃsāsūtrabhāṣya\" (The Commentary on the Mīmāṃsā Sūtras). Or simply \"Mīmāṃsā Bhāṣya\".\n\n33. id: \"f9127683-2df7-4863-9641-74f5e01220f4\", title: \"Mūlamadhyamakārikāḥ\"\n    This is the fundamental text of Mādhyamaka Buddhism by Nāgārjuna. Classification: buddhist. It is a philosophical treatise. Also could be considered a śāstra. Since it's a Buddhist text, code: buddhist.\n    Translation: Russian: \"Муламадхьямака-карики\", English: \"Mūlamadhyamakakārikā\" (Fundamental Verses on the Middle Way).\n\n34. id: \"055f03a4-89f7-4883-926f-900a05816953\", title: \"Mṛgendratantra\"\n    A Tantric text. Classification: tantra.\n    Translation: Russian: \"Мригендра-тантра\", English: \"The Mṛgendra Tantra\" (The Tantra of the Lord of Animals, i.e., Śiva?).\n\n35. id: \"53358f7f-54e4-4dda-b163-3dfecc3b0159\", title: \"Mṛgendraṭīkā\"\n    A commentary on the Mṛgendra Tantra. So classification: commentary, tika, tantra.\n    Translation: Russian: \"Тика на «Мригендра-тантру»\", English: \"The Ṭīkā on the Mṛgendra Tantra\".\n\n36. id: \"ca1962e9-e232-4032-9536-fbfa8da27d33\", title: \"Narasiṃhapurāṇa\"\n    A Purāṇa dedicated to Narasiṃha (the man-lion avatar). Classification: purana.\n    Translation: Russian: \"Нарасимха-пурана\", English: \"The Narasiṃha Purāṇa\".\n\n37. id: \"70c036a4-fa4e-469e-99d6-e4a5607b5b2f\", title: \"Narmamālā\"\n    \"Narma\" means \"sport, jest\", \"mālā\" garland. This could be a collection of humorous verses or a light-hearted poem. Classification: kavya (poetry), maybe shataka? Not exactly. I'll classify as kavya.\n    Translation: Russian: \"Нармамала\" (\"Гирлянда шуток\"), English: \"The Garland of Jests\" or \"The Chain of Humor\".\n\n38. id: \"68c42dc2-c1cc-43f0-821f-3e4ba9f86d2d\", title: \"Nibandhasaṃgraha\"\n    This means \"collection of nibandhas\" (digests or treatises). So it is a compilation of law digests or religious digests. Classification: nibandha, smriti? Since nibandhas often deal with dharma. So use nibandha, smriti.\n    Translation: Russian: \"Нибандха-санграха\" (\"Собрание рассуждений/трактатов\"), English: \"A Collection of Digests\" or \"Nibandhasaṃgraha\".\n\n39. id: \"2d389b1e-3766-49da-8558-4d566bd52fce\", title: \"Nighaṇṭuśeṣa\"\n    This is a supplement to the Nighaṇṭu (the Vedic lexicon by Yāska). So it's a nighantu, nirukta? Actually, it's part of the Nirukta tradition. Classification: nighantu, nirukta, vedanga (since Nirukta is a Vedāṅga).\n    Translation: Russian: \"Нигханту-шеша\" (\"Дополнение к Нигханту\"), English: \"The Supplemen t to the Nighaṇṭu\" or \"Nighaṇṭuśeṣa\".\n\n40. id: \"684374d4-f315-4fff-9211-c14e847d6c66\", title: \"Nirukta\"\n    Yāska's Nirukta, a commentary on the Nighaṇṭu and a treatise on etymology. Classification: nirukta, vedanga.\n    Translation: Russian: \"Нирукта\", English: \"Nirukta\".\n\n41. id: \"11ff1727-d8f4-47c6-b56c-d5146ccb38f7\", title: \"Nyāyabhāṣya\"\n    This is the Bhāṣya on the Nyāyasūtra by Vātsyāyana. Classification: nyaya, bhashya, commentary.\n    Translation: Russian: \"Ньяя-бхашья\", English: \"The Nyāyabhāṣya\" (The Commentary on the Nyāya Sūtras).\n\n42. id: \"002715f6-f675-4ec1-9a59-6966ebbaedbc\", title: \"Nyāyabindu\"\n    A Buddhist logical treatise by Dharmakīrti. Classification: buddhist, and it's a nyaya (logic) text. But since it's Buddhist logic, use buddhist, nyaya? We have both codes. So use: buddhist, nyaya.\n    Translation: Russian: \"Ньяя-бинду\" (\"Капля логики\"), English: \"The Drop of Logic\" or \"Nyāyabindu\".\n\n43. id: \"f1b4f911-7f76-41ae-abc4-8714785d8b71\", title: \"Nyāyasūtra\"\n    The foundational text of the Nyāya school by Gautama. Classification: nyaya, darshana (since it's a philosophical system). Use: nyaya.\n    Translation: Russian: \"Ньяя-сутры\", English: \"The Nyāya Sūtras\".\n\n44. id: \"14c70603-d15f-475f-86cc-79f37dee0b2b\", title: \"Nādabindūpaniṣat\"\n    A minor Upaniṣad, a Yoga Upaniṣad. Classification: upanishad, yoga (since it deals with nāda and bindu). Use: upanishad, yoga.\n    Translation: Russian: \"Нада-бинду-упанишада\", English: \"The Nādabindu Upaniṣad\".\n\n45. id: \"bac18679-91c8-4471-8aff-a04ba3732794\", title: \"Nāradasmṛti\"\n    A smṛti text by Nārada. Classification: smriti.\n    Translation: Russian: \"Нарада-смрити\", English: \"The Nārada Smṛti\".\n\n46. id: \"3143f36d-e1fb-447e-98c4-d14caf0920a2\", title: \"Nāḍīparīkṣā\"\n    This is a text on pulse examination, an Ayurvedic diagnostic method. Classification: ayurveda.\n    Translation: Russian: \"Нади-парикша\" (\"Исследование пульса\"), English: \"Examination of the Pulse\" or \"Nāḍīparīkṣā\".\n\n47. id: \"7910df8f-5c4a-4f33-ad07-4e2a86c2590d\", title: \"Nāṭyaśāstra\"\n    The foundational text on drama and performing arts by Bharata. Classification: nataka? Actually, it's a śāstra on nāṭya. We have \"nataka\" code for drama, but Nāṭyaśāstra is a treatise on dramaturgy. It can be classified under nataka or maybe kavya (since it's about poetry and drama). I'll use nataka, and also it's a śāstra. But we don't have a \"shastra\" code, but we can use \"nataka\" to indicate it's about drama. Some might classify as \"kavya\" but it's theoretical. I'll use \"nataka\".\n    Translation: Russian: \"Натьяшастра\", English: \"The Nāṭyaśāstra\" (The Treatise on Drama).\n\n48. id: \"1e19c8f7-da54-42db-90e6-3389f4ee8c4f\", title: \"Nāṭyaśāstravivṛti\"\n    A commentary on the Nāṭyaśāstra. Classification: commentary, vivriti (since it's a vivṛti), nataka (subject). So: commentary, vivriti, nataka.\n    Translation: Russian: \"Комментарий на «Натьяшастру»\", English: \"The Vivṛti on the Nāṭyaśāstra\" or \"Nāṭyaśāstravivṛti\".\n\n49. id: \"a777574c-e81b-4be9-9a61-901cfa010578\", title: \"Padārthacandrikā\"\n    This is a commentary. \"Padārtha\" means \"category, meaning of a word\", \"candrikā\" means \"moonlight\" (i.e., an illuminating commentary). It is often a title of a commentary on a grammatical or philosophical work. For example, there is a Padārthacandrikā on the Vākyapadīya or on a kośa. It could be a vyakarana or darshana commentary. Without more context, it's a commentary. Classification: commentary. Possibly vyakarana or nyaya? I'll use commentary.\n    Translation: Russian: \"Падартха-чандрика\" (\"Лунный свет категорий\"), English: \"The Moonlight on the Categories\" or \"Padārthacandrikā\".\n\n50. id: \"58011754-2306-4b2a-baec-fcdec1a845be\", title: \"Paramānandīyanāmamālā\"\n    This is a dictionary of synonyms or a thesaurus by Paramānanda. It's a kośa. \"Nāmamālā\" means \"garland of names\". So classification: kosha, nighantu? It's a type of nighaṇṭu. Use: kosha, nighantu.\n    Translation: Russian: \"Параманандия-намамала\", English: \"The Garland of Names by Paramānanda\" or \"Paramānandīyanāmamālā\".\n\nNow, I'll compile the JSON. Ensure all ids match and classification codes are arrays. Use the exact codes from the list.\n\nFor each, I'll output like:\n\n{\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"2c5a7983-2e2d-4dc3-8716-a0c75d641d22\",\n      \"title_sa_iast\": \"Kādambarīsvīkaraṇasūtramañjarī\",\n      \"title_ru\": \"Сутра-манджари о грамматическом использовании Кадамбари\",\n      \"title_en\": \"The Sutra Garland on the Grammatical Appropriation of Kādambarī\",\n      \"classification_codes\": [\"vyakarana\", \"commentary\"]\n    },\n    ... etc.\n  ]\n}\n\nI'll try to keep translations concise but meaningful. For well-known titles, I might use the standard English title.\n\nLet's produce final JSON.",
