lassification: aranyaka.\n\n9. Tantrasāra - A compendium of Tantra by Abhinavagupta or by Kṛṣṇānanda? Actually there are multiple texts named Tantrasāra. One is by Abhinavagupta, a summary of Tantrāloka. Another is a later Tantra compendium. Both are Tantra texts. So classification: tantra, agama. Possibly nibandha (compendium). But mainly tantra. I'll use tantra.\n\n10. Tantrākhyāyikā - A collection of stories, the original Pañcatantra? Tantrākhyāyikā is a recension of the Pañcatantra. It's narrative literature. Classification: katha (story). Also maybe itihasa? It's not itihasa, it's katha. So classification: katha.\n\n11. Tantrāloka - A major work on Kashmir Shaivism by Abhinavagupta. It's a Tantra text, a philosophical treatise on Tantra. Classification: tantra, agama, and also darshana? It's a Tantra philosophy. I'll use tantra, agama. Possibly also commentary? It's a synthesis. So tantra, agama.\n\n12. Tarkasaṃgraha - A primer on Nyāya-Vaiśeṣika by Annambhaṭṭa. It's a basic text on logic. Classification: nyaya, vaisheshika? Actually it covers both. It's a darshana text. I'll use nyaya, vaisheshika, darshana. But the code is nyaya, vaisheshika. Could also be considered a commentary? No, it's an original work. So classification: nyaya, vaisheshika.\n\n13. Tattvavaiśāradī - A commentary on the Yoga Bhāṣya by Vācaspati Miśra. It's a sub-commentary on Vyāsa's Bhāṣya on Yogasūtra. So classification: yoga, commentary, bhashya? Actually it's a vrtti? It's often called Tattvavaiśāradī, a commentary on the Yoga Bhāṣya. So it's a commentary. Use yoga, commentary, bhashya? It's a bhāṣya on a bhāṣya? Actually it's a vrtti on the Yoga Bhāṣya. So classification: yoga, vrtti. I'll use yoga, vrtti, commentary.\n\n14. Toḍalatantra - A Tantra text. Classification: tantra.\n\n15. Trikāṇḍaśeṣa - A supplement to the Trikāṇḍa (Amarakośa). It's a kośa (lexicon) by Puruṣottamadeva. So classification: kosha, nighantu? It's a kośa. So kosha.\n\n16. Uḍḍāmareśvaratantra - A Tantra text. Classification: tantra.\n\n17. Vaikhānasadharmasūtra - A Dharmasūtra of the Vaikhānasa school. Classification: dharmasutra, kalpa. Possibly also smriti. So dharmasutra.\n\n18. Vaikhānasagṛhyasūtra - A Gṛhyasūtra of the Vaikhānasa school. Classification: grihyasutra, kalpa.\n\n19. Vaikhānasaśrautasūtra - A Śrautasūtra of the Vaikhānasa school. Classification: shrautasutra, kalpa.\n\n20. Vaitānasūtra - A Śrautasūtra of the Atharvaveda. Classification: shrautasutra, kalpa.\n\n21. Vaiśeṣikasūtra - The foundational sūtra text of the Vaiśeṣika school, by Kaṇāda. Classification: vaisheshika, darshana.\n\n22. Vaiśeṣikasūtravṛtti - A commentary (vṛtti) on the Vaiśeṣikasūtra. Classification: vaisheshika, commentary, vrtti.\n\n23. Varāhapurāṇa - One of the major Purāṇas. Classification: purana.\n\n24. Vasiṣṭhadharmasūtra - A Dharmasūtra attributed to Vasiṣṭha. Classification: dharmasutra, kalpa, smriti.\n\n25. Vetālapañcaviṃśatikā - The twenty-five tales of the Vetāla (Vetāla stories). It's a story collection. Classification: katha.\n\n26. Viṃśatikākārikā - The verses of Vasubandhu's Viṃśatikā (Twenty Verses), a Buddhist Yogācāra text. Classification: buddhist, darshana? It's a Buddhist philosophical text. So buddhist. Also kārikā is a verse work. But classification: buddhist.\n\n27. Viṃśatikāvṛtti - Vasubandhu's own commentary on his Viṃśatikā. Classification: buddhist, commentary, vrtti.\n\n28. Viṣṇupurāṇa - One of the major Purāṇas. Classification: purana.\n\n29. Viṣṇusmṛti - A Dharmaśāstra text, one of the Smṛtis. Classification: smriti, dharmasutra? It's a Smṛti, so smriti.\n\n30. Vājasaneyisaṃhitā (Mādhyandina) - The Saṃhitā of the White Yajurveda, Mādhyandina recension. Classification: samhita.\n\n31. Vārāhagṛhyasūtra - A Gṛhyasūtra of the Vārāha school? Actually Vārāha Gṛhyasūtra is a text. Classification: grihyasutra, kalpa.\n\n32. Vārāhaśrautasūtra - A Śrautasūtra of the Vārāha school. Classification: shrautasutra, kalpa.\n\n33. Vātūlanāthasūtras - A text of the Nātha sect? Possibly a Tantra or Yoga text. Vātūlanātha is a Nātha teacher. The sūtras are probably a yoga/tantra text. Classification: yoga, tantra. I'll use yoga, tantra.\n\n34. Vātūlanāthasūtravṛtti - Commentary on the above. Classification: yoga, tantra, commentary, vrtti.\n\n35. Vṛddhayamasmṛti - A Smṛti text attributed to Vṛddha Yama (Old Yama). Classification: smriti.\n\n36. Yogaratnākara - A medical text on Yoga? Might be a text on Ayurveda or Yoga? Yogaratnākara is a well-known Ayurvedic text. It is a treatise on medicine. Classification: ayurveda. Possibly rasashastra? It includes alchemy? No, it's an Ayurvedic compendium. So ayurveda.\n\n37. Yogasūtra - The foundational text of Yoga by Patañjali. Classification: yoga, darshana.\n\n38. Yogasūtrabhāṣya - The commentary on Yogasūtra by Vyāsa. Classification: yoga, commentary, bhashya.\n\n39. Yājñavalkyasmṛti - A major Smṛti text. Classification: smriti.\n\n40. Ānandakanda - A text on Ayurveda or Rasashastra? Ānandakanda is a text on alchemy (Rasaśāstra). Classification: rasashastra, ayurveda? Actually it's a rasaśāstra text. So rasashastra.\n\n41. Āpastambadharmasūtra - A Dharmasūtra of the Āpastamba school. Classification: dharmasutra, kalpa.\n\n42. Āpastambagṛhyasūtra - A Gṛhyasūtra of Āpastamba. Classification: grihyasutra, kalpa.\n\n43. Āpastambaśrautasūtra - A Śrautasūtra of Āpastamba. Classification: shrautasutra, kalpa.\n\n44. Āryāsaptaśatī - A poem of 700 verses in Āryā meter by Govardhana. It's a kāvya. Classification: kavya, shataka? It's a śataka-like but 700 verses. It's a mahākāvya? Actually it's a collection of verses, a kāvya. I'll use kavya.\n\n45. Āyurvedadīpikā - A commentary on the Carakasaṃhitā. It's a commentary on Ayurveda. Classification: ayurveda, commentary. Possibly bhashya? It's a commentary. So ayurveda, commentary.\n\n46. Āśvalāyanagṛhyasūtra - A Gṛhyasūtra of Āśvalāyana. Classification: grihyasutra, kalpa.\n\n47. Āśvālāyanaśrautasūtra - A Śrautasūtra of Āśvalāyana. Classification: sh