assification: aranyaka.\n\n9. Tantrasāra - A compendium of Tantra by Abhinavagupta or by Kṛṣṇānanda? Actually there are multiple texts named Tantrasāra. One is by Abhinavagupta, a summary of Tantrāloka. Another is a later Tantra compendium. Both are Tantra texts. So classification: tantra, agama. Possibly nibandha (compendium). But mainly tantra. I'll use tantra.\n\n10. Tantrākhyāyikā - A collection of stories, the original Pañcatantra? Tantrākhyāyikā is a recension of the Pañcatantra. It's narrative literature. Classification: katha (story). Also maybe itihasa? It's not itihasa, it's katha. So classification: katha.\n\n11. Tantrāloka - A major work on Kashmir Shaivism by Abhinavagupta. It's a Tantra text, a philosophical treatise on Tantra. Classification: tantra, agama, and also darshana? It's a Tantra philosophy. I'll use tantra, agama. Possibly also commentary? It's a synthesis. So tantra, agama.\n\n12. Tarkasaṃgraha - A primer on Nyāya-Vaiśeṣika by Annambhaṭṭa. It's a basic text on logic. Classification: nyaya, vaisheshika? Actually it covers both. It's a darshana text. I'll use nyaya, vaisheshika, darshana. But the code is nyaya, vaisheshika. Could also be considered a commentary? No, it's an original work. So classification: nyaya, vaisheshika.\n\n13. Tattvavaiśāradī - A commentary on the Yoga Bhāṣya by Vācaspati Miśra. It's a sub-commentary on Vyāsa's Bhāṣya on Yogasūtra. So classification: yoga, commentary, bhashya? Actually it's a vrtti? It's often called Tattvavaiśāradī, a commentary on the Yoga Bhāṣya. So it's a commentary. Use yoga, commentary, bhashya? It's a bhāṣya on a bhāṣya? Actually it's a vrtti on the Yoga Bhāṣya. So classification: yoga, vrtti. I'll use yoga, vrtti, commentary.\n\n14. Toḍalatantra - A Tantra text. Classification: tantra.\n\n15. Trikāṇḍaśeṣa - A supplement to the Trikāṇḍa (Amarakośa). It's a kośa (lexicon) by Puruṣottamadeva. So classification: kosha, nighantu? It's a kośa. So kosha.\n\n16. Uḍḍāmareśvaratantra - A Tantra text. Cl