            "text": "We are asked: \"Return JSON only with exactly this structure: { \"results\": [ { \"id\": \"uuid_string_from_input\", \"title_sa_iast\": \"original_title\", \"title_ru\": \"translation_in_russian\", \"title_en\": \"translation_in_english\", \"classification_codes\": [\"code1\", \"code2\"] } ] }\". The input has a list of works. For each, we need to translate title to Russian and English, and assign classification codes from the provided list.\n\nLet's process each work:\n\n1. Abhidharmakośa: Buddhist philosophical text. Title: \"Abhidharma Treasury\" or similar. Russian: \"Сокровищница абхидхармы\". Classification: buddhist, darshana? It's a key Abhidharma text. So codes: buddhist, possibly darshana? But darshana is more for Hindu philosophies. So buddhist is appropriate. Also maybe kosha? But kosha is a category for lexicons. Not applicable. So just buddhist.\n\n2. Abhidharmakośabhāṣya: Commentary on above. Title: \"Commentary on the Abhidharma Treasury\". Russian: \"Комментарий к Сокровищнице абхидхармы\". Classification: buddhist, bhashya (commentary). So codes: buddhist, bhashya.\n\n3. Abhidhānacintāmaṇi: A lexicon of synonymous words. Title: \"Wish-granting gem of synonyms\". Russian: \"Чинтамани синонимов\" or more literally \"Драгоценность размышлений о словах\"? Actually Abhidhāna means \"word, designation\", Cintāmaṇi is wish-fulfilling gem. So English: \"Wish-fulfilling Gem of Nouns/Synonyms\". It's a kośa (lexicon). So classification: kosha, nighantu (since nighantu is a kind of lexicon). So codes: kosha, nighantu.\n\n4. Abhinavacintāmaṇi: A medical text? Abhinava means \"new\", Cintāmaṇi \"wish-gem\". Possibly a medical treatise? Actually it's a text on Ayurveda maybe. Let me check: Abhinavacintāmaṇi is a work on medicine? I recall it's an Ayurvedic text. Classification: ayurveda. Also maybe rasashastra? But likely ayurveda. So ayurveda.\n\n5. Acintyastava: A praise hymn. \"Acintya\" means inconceivable, \"stava\" praise. So \"Inconce