les, which often have \"rasa\" as a prefix. Here \"rasika\" is the enjoyer. So I'll assume it's on poetics or aesthetics. So classification: [\"kāvya\"] or maybe it's a stotra? I'll go with [\"kāvya\"] for now. But wait, Keśavadāsa's Rasikapriyā is in Brajbhasha, not Sanskrit. There might be a Sanskrit Rasikapriyā. I'll consider it a work on poetics. English: \"Beloved of the Connoisseur\". Russian: \"Возлюбленная ценителя\".\n\n14. Rasikasaṃjīvanī: \"Rasika-saṃjīvanī\" - \"Reviver of the connoisseur\" or \"Elixir for the connoisseur\". Similarly, likely a commentary on something aesthetic? There is a well-known commentary on the Rāmāyaṇa called \"Tilaka\" or \"Bhoja's commentary\"? Actually, there is a \"Rāmāyaṇa\" commentary \"Rasikasaṃjīvanī\"? I'm not sure. I think there is a \"Rasikasaṃjīvanī\" by Raghunātha? It might be a commentary on the Bhāgavata Purāṇa or on alchemy. Again, the word \"rasika\" suggests aesthetics. Possibly a commentary on a poetical work. I'll classify as [\"commentary\", \"kāvya\"] perhaps. But to be consistent, if Rasikapriyā is kāvya, Rasikasaṃjīvanī might be a commentary on a kāvya. So codes: [\"commentary\", \"kāvya\"]. English: \"Reviving of the Connoisseur\". Russian: \"Оживление ценителя\". Or \"Эликсир для ценителя\".\n\n15. Rasādhyāya: \"Rasa-adhyāya\" - \"Chapter on Rasa\". This is likely a chapter from some larger work, possibly on alchemy or medicine. Could be from a Āyurvedic text. Classify as [\"rasaśāstra\"] if alchemical, or maybe [\"āyurveda\"] if medical. I think it's alchemical. I'll use [\"rasaśāstra\"]. Translation: \"Chapter on Rasa\". Russian: \"Глава о расе\".\n\n16. Rasādhyāyaṭīkā: \"Commentary on the Rasādhyāya\". So commentary on the above. Classify: [\"commentary\", \"rasaśāstra\"]. English: \"Commentary on the Chapter on Rasa\". Russian: \"Комментарий к главе о расе\".\n\n17. Rasārṇava: \"Rasa-arṇava\" - \"Ocean of Rasa\". Alchemical. Classify: [\"rasaśāstra\"]. English: \"Ocean of Rasa\". Russian: \"Океан расы\".\n\n18. Rasārṇavakalpa: \"Rasārṇava-kalpa\" - \"Ritual of the Ocean of Rasa\" or \"Section of the Ocean of Rasa\". \"Kalpa\" can mean ritual or section. Probably an alchemical text. Classify: [\"rasaśāstra\"]. English: \"Ritual of the Ocean of Rasa\" or \"Kalpa of the Ocean of Rasa\". Russian: \"Кальпа океана расы\". I'll translate as \"Ритуал океана расы\".\n\n19. Ratnadīpikā: \"Ratna-dīpikā\" - \"Illumination of Gems\". This could be a commentary on some gemological or alchemical text, or on a philosophical text. There is a \"Ratnadīpikā\" commentary on the Bhagavadgītā? Or on the Brahmasūtra? Not sure. But in the context of alchemy, it might be a commentary on a gem text. I'll check other titles: earlier we had alchemical texts with \"ratna\" (gem). So likely it's a commentary on some text dealing with gems, which falls under rasaśāstra. So classify: [\"commentary\", \"rasaśāstra\"]. English: \"Illumination of Gems\". Russian: \"Освещение драгоценных камней\".\n\n20. Ratnaṭīkā: \"Ratna-ṭīkā\" - \"Commentary on Gems\". Commentary. Classify: [\"commentary\", \"rasaśāstra\"]. English: \"Commentary on Gems\". Russian: \"Комментарий к драгоценным камням\".\n\n21. Rājamārtaṇḍa: \"Rāja-mārtaṇḍa\" - \"King of the Sun\" or \"Royal Sun\". This is a famous commentary on the Yogasūtra by Bhoja? Actually, Bhoja's commentary on Yogasūtra is called \"Rājamārtaṇḍa\". Yes, that's correct. So classify as [\"commentary\", \"yoga\"]. English: \"Royal Sun\". Russian: \"Царственное солнце\". It's a commentary on Yogasūtra, so yoga.\n\n22. Rājanighaṇṭu: \"Rāja-nighaṇṭu\" - \"Royal Nighaṇṭu\". Nighaṇṭu is a glossary, especially of medicinal plants. There is a famous \"Rājanighaṇṭu\" by Narahari Pandita, an Ayurvedic lexicon. So classify as [\"āyurveda\", \"nighaṇṭu\"]. Actually, the code \"nighaṇṭu\" is available. So codes: [\"nighaṇṭu\", \"āyurveda\"]? Since it's a medical glossary. I'll use both. English: \"Royal Nighantu\". Russian: \"Царственный нигханту\".\n\n23. Rāmāyaṇa: The epic. Classify as [\"itihāsa\"]. Indeed, Rāmāyaṇa is itihāsa. English: \"The Rāmāyaṇa\". Russian: \"Рамаяна\".\n\n24. Saddharmapuṇḍarīkasūtra: Buddhist text, the Lotus Sutra. Classify as [\"buddhist\"]. English: \"Sutra of the White Lotus of the True Dharma\". Russian: \"Сутра белого лотоса истинной дхармы\". Actually, \"Saddharmapuṇḍarīka\" means \"Lotus of the True Law\". So translation: \"Lotus Sutra of the True Law\" or \"Sutra of the Lotus of the Wonderful Law\". Common English: \"Lotus Sutra\". I'll put \"Lotus Sutra of the True Dharma\". Russian: \"Сутра лотоса истинной дхармы\".\n\n25. Sarvadarśanasaṃgraha: \"Compendium of all philosophical systems\" by Mādhava. Classify as [\"darshana\"]? It's a compendium of various darśanas. So code \"darshana\" is appropriate as a general category. Could also be considered a \"samgraha\" (collection) but we have nibandha? Actually, it's a compendium, so maybe \"darshana\" is fine. The code \"darshana\" means philosophical system. So I'll use [\"darshana\"]. English: \"Compendium of All Philosophical Systems\". Russian: \"Собрание всех философских систем\".\n\n26. Sarvāṅgasundarā: \"Beautiful in all limbs\". This is a commentary on the Amarakośa? I recall \"Sarvāṅgasundarā\" is a commentary on the Amarakośa by Gopāla Kavirāja? Or on the Aṣṭādhyāyī? Actually, \"Sarvāṅgasundarā\" is a commentary on the Amarakośa by Vandyaghaṭīya Sarvānanda? There is a famous commentary on the Amarakośa called \"Sarvāṅgasundarā\" by Gopāla Bhāṣya? Let me think: The Amarakośa has commentaries like \"Vyākhyāsudhā\", \"Sarvāṅgasundarā\" by Bhaṭṭoji Dīkṣita? No, Bhaṭṭoji wrote \"Śabdakaustubha\". I think \"Sarvāṅgasundarā\" is a commentary on the Amarakośa. So classify as [\"commentary\", \"kosha\"]. English: \"Beautiful in All Limbs\". Russian: \"Прекрасная во всех частях\". Actually, translation: \"Всецело прекрасная\". But I'll give \"Прекрасная всеми членами\".\n\n27. Saundarānanda: \"Saundara-ānanda\" - \"Beautiful Nanda\"? Actually, it's a Buddhist text: \"Saundarananda\" by Aśvaghoṣa, a kāvya about Nanda. Classify as [\"kavya\"]? It's a mahākāvya? Actually, Aśvaghoṣa's works are kāvya. I'd classify as [\"kavya\"] or more specifically [\"mahākāvya\"]? It's an epic poem, so mahākāvya. But our list has \"mahākāvya\" as a code. So I'll use [\"mahākāvya\"]. English: \"Saundarananda\" or \"The Beautiful Nanda\". Russian: \"Саундарананда\" (or \"Прекрасный Нанда\"). I'll put \"Прекрасный Нанда\".\n\n28. Saṃvitsiddhi: \"Saṃvit-siddhi\" - \"Attainment of Consciousness\". This is likely a philosophical text, possibly from the Kashmir Shaivism or Vedanta. There is a text \"Saṃvitsiddhi\" by unknown? I think it's a tantric or Shaiva text. Classify as [\"tantra\"] or [\"darshana\"]? I'll check: \"Saṃvitsiddhi\" might be part of the Śaiva Āgamas. So classify as [\"āgama\"] or [\"tantra\"]. Since we have \"agama\" and \"tantra\", I'll go with [\"tantra\"] if it's a Tantric work. English: \"Attainment of Consciousness\". Russian: \"Достижение сознания\".\n\n29. Saṅghabhedavastu: \"Saṅgha-bheda-vastu\" - \"The Case of the Schism in the Order\". This is a Buddhist text, part of the Vinaya. Classify as [\"buddhist\"]. English: \"The Story of the Schism in the Order\". Russian: \"Случай раскола в сангхе\".\n\n30. Skandapurāṇa: One of the Mahāpurāṇas. Classify as [\"purana\"]. English: \"Skanda Purāṇa\". Russian: \"Сканда-пурана\".\n\n31. Skandapurāṇa (Revākhaṇḍa): A specific section of the Skandapurāṇa. Still a purana. Classify: [\"purana\"]. Translation: \"Skanda Purāṇa (Revākhaṇḍa)\". Russian: \"Сканда-пурана (Рева-кханда)\". Note: \"Revākhaṇḍa\" means \"Section of the Revā river\".\n\n32. Smaradīpikā: \"Smara-dīpikā\" - \"Lamp of Love\" or \"Illumination of Desire\". This is a text on erotics? Or a commentary on Kāmasūtra? I think \"Smaradīpikā\" is a work on sexual love, part of Kāmaśāstra. But we don't have a specific code for kāmaśāstra. The closest might be \"tantra\" if it's tantric, or \"kavya\"? Actually, it's a text on erotics, so maybe \"tantra\"? Or \"smriti\"? Not sure. I recall \"Smaradīpikā\" is a work on erotics. Could be classified under \"kama\" (but not in our list). The available codes include \"tantra\" (since some tantras deal with this). Alternatively, it might be considered a commentary on Kāmasūtra, so \"commentary\". I'll check: \"Smaradīpikā\" by Ānanda? Or it might be a work on Ayurveda? No, it's about love. I'll classify it as [\"tantra\"] if it's part of Tantric literature, but I'm not 100% sure. Another possibility: it's a \"kavya\" if it's poetry about love. But the title \"dīpikā\" often indicates a commentary. There is a \"Smaradīpikā\" by Vaidya? I think it's a standalone text on erotics. I'll use [\"tantra\"] for now, since many such texts are considered Tantric. Alternatively, it could be \"smriti\"? I'll go with [\"tantra\"]. English: \"Lamp of Love\". Russian: \"Светильник любви\".\n\n33. Spandakārikā: \"Spanda-kārikā\" - \"Verses on Vibration\". This is a Kashmiri Shaiva text, foundational. Classify as [\"tantra\"] or [\"agama\"]? It's a Śāstra of the Spanda school. I'll use [\"tantra\"] because it's part of the Tantric tradition. English: \"Spandakārikā\" or \"Verses on Vibration\". Russian: \"Спанда-карики\" (\"Строфы о вибрации\").\n\n34. Spandakārikānirṇaya: \"Spandakārikā-nirṇaya\" - \"Ascertainment of the Spandakārikā\". A commentary on the Spandakārikā. Classify as [\"commentary\", \"tantra\"]. English: \"Ascertainment of the Spandakārikā\". Russian: \"Определение Спанда-карик\".\n\n35. Sphuṭārthāvyākhyā: \"Sphuṭa-artha-vyākhyā\" - \"Commentary on the Clear Meaning\". This is a commentary on something? Possibly on the Amarakośa? I recall \"Sphuṭārthā\" is a commentary on the Amarakośa? Actually, there is a commentary on the Amarakośa called \"Sphuṭārthā\". Or it could be on a grammar text. I'll check: \"Sphuṭārthā\" is a commentary on the Amarakośa by Vandyaghaṭīya Sarvānanda? No, that's \"Sarvāṅgasundarā\". \"Sphuṭārthā\" is a commentary on the Amarakośa by Raghunātha? Not sure. Alternatively, it might be a commentary on a philosophical text. Given the name, it's a commentary. I'll classify as [\"commentary\"] and maybe [\"kosha\"] if on the Amarakośa. I'll go with [\"commentary\"] generically, but since I'm not sure of the subject, I'll just use [\"commentary\"]. However, many commentaries in this list are on specific subjects. I think \"Sphuṭārthāvyākhyā\" is a commentary on the \"Amarakośa\"? There is a well-known commentary \"Sphuṭārthā\" on the Amarakośa by Bhaṭṭa Kṣīrasvāmin? Or is it \"Sphuṭārthā\" by Sarvānanda? Actually, the Amarakośa has the commentary \"Sphuṭārthā\" by Bhaṭṭoji Dīkṣita? Not likely. I'll check my memory: The Amarakośa commentaries include \"Vyākhyāsudhā\", \"Sarvāṅgasundarā\", \"Padachandas\" etc. I think \"Sphuṭārthā\" is a commentary on the Aṣṭādhyāyī? No. I'll assume it's a commentary on the Amarakośa based on a vague recollection. So I'll add [\"kosha\"] too. But to be safe, I'll just use [\"commentary\"] and omit the subject if uncertain. However, the instructions: \"If uncertain, provide your best guess and include all possible classifications.\" So I'll add [\"commentary\"] and maybe [\"kosha\"]. I'll add both [\"commentary\", \"kosha\"]? Actually, the work might be a vyākhyā (commentary) and the subject is kosha (lexicon). So yes, I'll classify as [\"commentary\", \"kosha\"]. English: \"Commentary on the Clear Meaning\" (or \"Clear Meaning Commentary\"). Russian: \"Комментарий к ясному значению\".\n\n36. Suśrutasaṃhitā: Ancient medical text. Classify as [\"ayurveda\"]. Also it's a samhita, but the code \"samhita\" is for Vedic samhitas. Suśruta is not Vedic, it's an Ayurvedic samhita. So use [\"ayurveda\"]. English: \"Suśruta's Compendium\". Russian: \"Сушрута-самхита\".\n\n37. Sāmavidhānabrāhmaṇa: A Brāhmaṇa text of the Sāmaveda. Classify as [\"brahmana\"]. English: \"Brāhmaṇa of the Sāma Rituals\". Russian: \"Самавидхана-брахмана\". Actually, \"Sāmavidhāna\" is a text of the Sāmaveda, it's a Brāhmaṇa. So I'll classify as [\"brahmana\"]. Translation: \"Sāmavidhāna Brāhmaṇa\". Russian: \"Самавидхана-брахмана\".\n\n38. Sātvatatantra: A Tantric text of the Pāñcarātra tradition? \"Sātvata\" is a term related to Vaishnava tantras. There is a \"Sātvatatantra\" which is a Vaishnava tantra. Classify as [\"tantra\"]. English: \"Sātvata Tantra\". Russian: \"Сатвата-тантра\".\n\n39. Sāṃkhyakārikā: Foundational text of Sāṃkhya philosophy, by Īśvarakṛṣṇa. Classify as [\"samkhya\"]. English: \"Sāṃkhyakārikā\". Russian: \"Санкхья-карики\".\n\n40. Sāṃkhyakārikābhāṣya: Commentary on the Sāṃkhyakārikā, likely by Gauḍapāda or Vācaspatimiśra? Actually, Gauḍapāda's commentary is called \"Sāṃkhyakārikābhāṣya\". So classify as [\"commentary\", \"samkhya\"]. English: \"Commentary on the Sāṃkhyakārikā\". Russian: \"Комментарий к Санкхья-карикам\".\n\n41. Sāṃkhyatattvakaumudī: Another commentary on the Sāṃkhyakārikā, by Vācaspati Miśra. Classify as [\"commentary\", \"samkhya\"]. English: \"Sāṃkhyatattvakaumudī\" (Moonlight of the Sāṃkhya Truth). Russian: \"Санкхья-таттва-каумуди\" (\"Лунный свет истины санкхьи\").\n\n42. Sūryasiddhānta: An astronomical text. Classify as [\"jyotisha\"]. English: \"Sūrya Siddhānta\". Russian: \"Сурья-сиддханта\".\n\n43. Sūryaśataka: A \"śataka\" (century of verses) in praise of Sūrya, by Mayūra? Actually, Mayūra wrote \"Sūryaśataka\". So it's a stotra or kāvya. Classify as [\"stotra\", \"shataka\"]? Both codes exist. \"śataka\" is a genre of 100 verses. So [\"shataka\"] is appropriate, and it's a stotra as well. So [\"shataka\", \"stotra\"]. English: \"Century of Verses for Sūrya\". Russian: \"Сурья-шатака\" (\"Сто строф Сурье\").\n\n44. Sūryaśatakaṭīkā: Commentary on the above. Classify: [\"commentary\", \"shataka\", \"stotra\"]. English: \"Commentary on the Sūryaśataka\". Russian: \"Комментарий к Сурья-шатаке\".\n\n45. Taittirīyabrāhmaṇa: The Brāhmaṇa of the Taittirīya school of the Yajurveda. Classify as [\"b